# GUTTERCAPS API — every variable the backend reads.
#
# Start here, not in the source: this file is generated from the code (see the marker below), so the
# list is complete, and the sections above it are the parts that actually decide whether a deploy
# works. Nothing here has a secret in it — copy to `backend/.env`, set the marked ones, leave the rest.
#
# ── required, no safe default ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   SESSION_SECRET        ≥ 32 chars. Ephemeral per process when unset, so a restart would log every
#                         player out and invalidate a session mid-transaction.
#   SIWS_DOMAINS          the sign-in-text domain allowlist (`app.guttercaps.gg`).
#   ADMIN_WALLETS         comma-separated base58; empty = /admin/* is closed (that is the safe state).
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET      required in production unless HUMAN_CHECK=0 is set on purpose (docs/06 §2.1).
#   TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES   the domains a siteverify token is allowed to come from, comma-separated, leading
#                         dot = that domain and its subdomains (`.guttercaps.gg` covers app + www). The
#                         sitekey is public, so WITHOUT this list any page on any domain can mint a token
#                         and hand out 7-day human passes; in production an empty list refuses to boot
#                         (SEC-B5). Set this even when testing — it is the whole control.
#   TURNSTILE_ACTION      must equal the action the widget sends (`claim`, see HumanCheck.tsx); empty means
#                         "any action", which only makes sense in a dev sandbox.
# ── cluster split (never one value for both) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   PROGRAM_*             four program ids. Defaults are the dev placeholders; the real ones come from
#                         `npm run program-ids -- apply` at the freeze commit (docs/09 §2).
#   SOLANA_RPC_URL        mainnet RPC for the API; the listener needs one with websocket support.
#   USDC_MINT / SKR_MINT  resolved by address, never by symbol — counterfeits exist.
# ── prod fail-fast ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `NODE_ENV=production` makes a wrong combination *refuse to boot* rather than degrade quietly
# (`assertProductionConfig` in src/config.ts): wildcard CORS, missing COOKIE_SECURE, short session
# secret, missing/ephemeral DB_PATH, PRODUCTION_DB_MODE unset, EVENT_BUS=redis without REDIS_URL, FINALITY_ASSUME=1, a crank hot key
# equal to the localnet id. Read that list before adding a check of your own.

